@startuml Support Flow

title Real-time Support Chat Flow

actor Student
actor Instructor
participant "WebSocket" as WS
participant "Support Service" as SS
participant "Notification Service" as NT
participant "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "RabbitMQ" as RMQ

== Create Support Session ==
Student -> WS: SEND /app/support/sessions/create\n{initialMessage}
WS -> SS: createSession(studentId, email, name, message)

SS -> DB: Save session and initial message
DB --> SS: Saved

SS -> RMQ: Publish SupportRequestedEvent\n{sessionId, studentId, email, name, message}
RMQ -> NT: Consume SupportRequestedEvent
NT -> Instructor: Send email/push notification

WS -> Student: SEND /topic/support\nWebSocketMessage.NEW_SESSION
WS -> Instructor: SEND /topic/support\nWebSocketMessage.NEW_SESSION

== Instructor Joins Session ==
Instructor -> WS: SUBSCRIBE /topic/support/sessions/{sessionId}
WS -> SS: getSessionById(sessionId, userPrincipal)

SS -> DB: Retrieve session and mark messages as read
DB --> SS: Session data

WS -> Instructor: SEND /topic/support/{sessionId}\nWebSocketMessage.SESSION_JOINED
WS -> Student: SEND /topic/support\nWebSocketMessage.SESSION_JOINED

== Send Message ==
Instructor -> WS: SEND /app/support/sessions/{sessionId}/messages/send\n{content}
WS -> SS: sendMessage(userPrincipal, sessionId, request)

SS -> DB: Save message and assign instructor if needed
DB --> SS: Message saved

WS -> Student: SEND /topic/support\nWebSocketMessage.NEW_MESSAGE
WS -> Instructor: SEND /topic/support/{sessionId}\nWebSocketMessage.NEW_MESSAGE

== Close Session ==
Student -> WS: SEND /app/support/sessions/{sessionId}/close
WS -> SS: closeSession(sessionId, userId)

SS -> DB: Close session
DB --> SS: Session updated

WS -> Student: SEND /topic/support/{sessionId}\nWebSocketMessage.SESSION_CLOSED
WS -> Instructor: SEND /topic/support\nWebSocketMessage.SESSION_CLOSED

@enduml
